# Offline fallback quit password for Safe Exam Browser (CBT Edition)
#
# Place this file (renamed to "CbtFallback.txt") in one of:
#     C:\ProgramData\SafeExamBrowser\CbtFallback.txt   (all users - preferred, needs admin rights)
#     C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Roaming\SafeExamBrowser\CbtFallback.txt
#
# It is only used when NO CBT kiosk endpoint is reachable (server down / no internet).
# When the CBT server answers, the password from the CBT panel always wins.
#
# Lines starting with '#' are comments. Use ONE of the two keys below.

# --- Recommended: Base16 (lowercase hex) SHA-256 hash of the emergency password ------
# Get the hash, e.g. in PowerShell:
#     $p='MyEmergencyPassword'; $s=[Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($p)
#     ([BitConverter]::ToString((New-Object Security.Cryptography.SHA256Managed).ComputeHash($s)) -replace '-','').ToLower()
password_hash=

# --- Alternative: plain-text password (less secure, stored readable) -----------------
# password=MyEmergencyPassword
